<title>UK: Zhenhai prices $200 mln convertible.</title>
<headline>Zhenhai prices $200 mln convertible.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Zhenhai Refining &amp; Chemical Co Ltd has set a HK$2.80 conversion price on its $200 million convertible bond, joint lead managers ING Barings and Morgan Stanley said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The conversion price represents a 12 percent premium over the five-day average. The coupon was fixed at 3.00 percent.</p>
<p>There is a put after five years years which was priced to yield 80 basis points over U.S. Treasuries.</p>
<p>Atlantic Richfield Co will buy $128 million, or 64 percent, of the London and Hong Kong-listed issue.</p>
<p>-- Dan Lalor, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
